    {
      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "To solve this problem, let's first define what the complement of an angle is. The complement of an angle is the angle that, when added to the given angle, equals 90 degrees. Therefore, if the measure of the angle is \\( x \\) degrees, then its complement is \\( 90 - x \\) degrees.\n\nThe problem states that the measure of the angle is double the measure of its complement. This can be expressed as:\n\\[ x = 2(90 - x) \\]\n\nNow, let's solve for \\( x \\) step by step:\n1. Distribute the 2 on the right side of the equation:\n\\[ x = 180 - 2x \\]\n\n2. Add \\( 2x \\) to both sides to get all \\( x \\) terms on one side:\n\\[ x + 2x = 180 \\]\n\\[ 3x = 180 \\]\n\n3. Divide both sides by 3 to solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{180}{3} \\]\n\\[ x = 60 \\]\n\nSo, the degree measure of the angle is \\( 60 \\) degrees.",
