      "text": "Let the measure of the angle be \\( x \\) degrees. The complement of this angle is \\( 90 - x \\) degrees. According to the problem, the angle is double the measure of its complement. This relationship can be expressed as:\n\\[ x = 2(90 - x) \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( x \\), we can expand and simplify the equation:\n\\[ x = 180 - 2x \\]\n\\[ x + 2x = 180 \\]\n\\[ 3x = 180 \\]\n\\[ x = 60 \\]\n\nSo, the measure of the angle is \\( 60 \\) degrees. We can verify this by checking that \\( 60 \\) degrees is indeed double the measure of its complement, which is \\( 30 \\) degrees. Let's write the Python code to verify this solution.\n\n```python\n# Define the angle x\nx = 60\n\n# Calculate the complement of the angle\ncomplement = 90 - x\n\n# Check if the angle is double the measure of its complement\nis_double = x == 2 * complement\n\nprint((x, complement, is_double))\n```\n```output\n(60, 30, True)\n```\nThe output confirms that the measure of the angle is \\( 60 \\) degrees, and it is indeed double the measure of its complement (which is \\( 30 \\) degrees). Therefore, the degree measure of the angle is \\(\\boxed{60}\\).",
